<title>POLAND: NFI units close higher in live trade.</title>
<headline>NFI units close higher in live trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish mass privatisation NFI units closed at 124 zlotys in Warsaw bourse continuous trade on Tuesday, 9.1 percent higher than at their opening price.</p>
<p>Turnover was at 7.9 million zlotys versus 2.6 million on Monday.</p>
<p>The five stocks in the continuous system -- BIG, BPH, Debica, Elektrim and Rolimpex -- did not trade.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
